From: Seeed Rockchip BSP
Subject: [PATCH] pxe: expand environment macros in the FDT directive

cmd/pxe.c runs the APPEND directive (and, with the FDTOVERLAYS change,
the overlay list) through cli_simple_process_macros(), but uses the FDT
file name exactly as it was parsed.  A board that picks its device tree
at boot time - e.g. from a board ID EEPROM, so that one extlinux.conf on
a read-only rootfs serves several board variants of the same SoC -
cannot express that as ${...}: the literal text is handed to the loader
as a file name and the boot stops with "Skipping ... for failure
retrieving fdt".

Expand the directive the same way APPEND is expanded.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/cmd/pxe.c	2026-09-22 10:12:00.000000000 +0800
+++ b/cmd/pxe.c	2026-09-22 10:12:00.000000000 +0800
@@ -825,7 +825,18 @@
 		char *fdtfilefree = NULL;

 		if (label->fdt) {
-			fdtfile = label->fdt;
+			/*
+			 * Expand ${...} macros, exactly like the APPEND and
+			 * FDTOVERLAYS directives.  The FDT file name can then
+			 * come from the environment - e.g. selected at boot
+			 * time from a board ID EEPROM - so a single
+			 * extlinux.conf on a read-only rootfs serves several
+			 * board variants of the same SoC.
+			 */
+			char fdt_buf[CONFIG_SYS_CBSIZE];
+
+			cli_simple_process_macros(label->fdt, fdt_buf);
+			fdtfile = fdt_buf;
 		} else if (label->fdtdir) {
 			char *f1, *f2, *f3, *f4, *slash;

